  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_80fe417b5c5449cebe1308c4e576c22e",
      "statement": "L2 domain verification anchors the listed pseudonym to a domain the key holder controls; the directory performs the control check itself over a single-use challenge token using one of two methods (dns_txt and https_well_known), and the resulting trust signal is labelled domain_verified — a control fact with method and timestamps, never KYC or \"verified business\".",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/SPEC.md#L246-L253",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e7aea8ab5d89703ea001b524bb1dfacfac80e38dc90a799e119f673576247d36:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/domain.py#L1-L7",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9592c0d7f7ade1f1066e468e65c5bfbdb383047d6c4b3dbd821f675a88728cc4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9dd7418b82674dc393c9814eb88face7",
      "statement": "POST /v1/verify-domain (202) calls DomainService.request_verification: it requires a currently listed, non-expired agent (AGENT_NOT_LISTED), validates the claimed domain (DOMAIN_INVALID) and the method (only dns_txt or https_well_known, else INVALID_SCHEMA), verifies the agent's signature over the canonical JSON subset (fingerprint, domain, method), and mints verification_id 'vd_' + token_hex(16) plus a 256-bit single-use token bound to the fingerprint, returning token, instructions, expires_at and ttl_seconds.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/domain.py#L59-L103",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f9cac624166904743dc73973e7e5fa4aca6eb1236416becb65dd7025d8ee0d32:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/http_api.py#L395-L402",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d85760c2a555a9c6d73ea31f4862094cae2758ee2ace9edcbb8d7a757e05d6e1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7e0452932f0b45cfbff7bb920ca1622e",
      "statement": "POST /v1/verify-domain/confirm (200) calls DomainService.confirm in a strict order: live-agent check, signature over the subset (fingerprint, verification_id), challenge lookup that rejects unknown/foreign challenges as VERIFICATION_NOT_FOUND (404), already-used as VERIFICATION_USED (409) and past-TTL as VERIFICATION_EXPIRED (410), then endpoint match, then the server-side control probe; on success the challenge is consumed and a 90-day verification persisted in one store transaction.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/domain.py#L105-L150",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e354c5d5d37b268cce02e14e68287a8fe3f992dc1f00ba7fbeb9477e8dd59307:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/store.py#L614-L661",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dd4ce6cf87d2e18f219d47c2cf383cb7eede77837c2db2ee20c3fece6e687b76:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2b986509db344e8f98116d53a02f021f",
      "statement": "The directory never trusts an agent's claim of success: confirm delegates the actual control probe to an injected Resolver seam (SystemResolver in production dispatches to verify.check_dns_txt / verify.check_https_well_known) and only a passing probe can persist the signal; a failed probe raises a stable DirectoryError code and does not consume the challenge, so confirm is retryable with the same verification_id until the token TTL expires.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/domain.py#L152-L155",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:723cfc73b7225c341292342b17ed317e6f5262c3abbadfa04fb6a13fcc81f3f9:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/resolver.py#L22-L34",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1ab741c4d4bb2dae2b17e2aa853c03267f53e22248cfc9000d5edc20fe8cfa02:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_domain_verification.py#L94-L117",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:30b5ce176119e8f2630fdb9de9ab94b6bc8dd117ab8cc9834eb7d6da67bd047e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a305ce6f9b4249c8899e4b53052d8ead",
      "statement": "The dns_txt check (check_dns_txt) shells out to the system dig binary with 'dig +noall +answer TXT _haap.<domain>' and a 10 s timeout, accepts a TXT record whose value equals the token or starts with 'haap-verify=<token>', treats an answer CNAME whose target leaves the approximated two-label registrable domain as DNS_TXT_NOT_FOUND (422), and maps a missing, failed, or timed-out dig to DNS_ERROR_TEMPORARY (503).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/verify.py#L73-L113",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:900f072189ee2ddc2cbac410033cf59d8022a1ac87bf1cc3f6d21a1b0b034d21:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_25d63308c47f458ba975cf9c0ecec600",
      "statement": "The https_well_known check (check_https_well_known) fetches https://<domain>/.well-known/haap-verify.txt over stdlib TLS (falling back to the .json variant only on a .txt 404) with a 10 s timeout and a 4 KiB + 1 read cap; redirects are followed only when every hop is https and stays within the original domain's registrable domain; success requires the trimmed body to equal the token or, for JSON, the field haap_verify_token; failures raise WELL_KNOWN_NOT_FOUND or WELL_KNOWN_MISMATCH (both 422).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/verify.py#L116-L175",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4d199c481a942412df5362f78922d6c9d1d6ac145c9224eee3d395a88999ff82:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2cc6c990d04e441084fd5c8984699f9d",
      "statement": "validate_domain normalizes to a stripped, lowercase bare hostname and rejects scheme/port/path/userinfo, whitespace, length over 253, fewer than two labels, or a format outside the label regex — all as DOMAIN_INVALID (400); registrable_domain approximates the registrable domain as the last two labels (deliberately conservative for multi-label public suffixes) and gates both the DNS CNAME rule and the well-known redirect cage.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/verify.py#L40-L70",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1c161aa2580378687068d30e0bf521adf0ba671b43d454b474266c080069ef32:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_39b4b8ac88904917bba8aa7a88e8ed79",
      "statement": "confirm requires the stored manifest's agent.endpoint host to equal the claimed domain or be a subdomain of it (endpoint_host + host_under_domain), raising DOMAIN_ENDPOINT_MISMATCH (422) before any resolver or network activity; the same subdomain relation selects the primary verification among an agent's possibly several verified domains.",
